  "name": null,
  "problem": "The owner of a fast food stall wants to check the strength of the linear correlation between the following variables:\n\n- $x,$ the price per bag of onion rings, in dollars, and\n\n- $y,$ the number of bags of onion rings sold that day.\n\nYou are given that $\\text{Cov}(x,y)=-5,$ ${\\sigma }_{x}=1,$ and ${\\sigma }_{y}=6.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\rho ≈-0.83$\n\nII. There is a strong negative correlation between $x$ and $y.$\n\nIII. There is a weak negative correlation between $x$ and $y.$\n\n*Hint: $|\\rho |>0.7$ indicates a strong correlation, and $0.3\\le |\\rho |\\le 0.7$ indicates a weak correlation.*",
  "worked_solution": "",
